-# Rhythmer quickstart
+# Rhythmer OS quickstart
 
-This guide takes you from the release zip to a saved beat with a kit and a
-plug-in instrument. For every page and control, read the
-[user guide](GUIDE.md).
+Load a sample kit or choose one of the 20 instruments from PLUG-INS. Rhythmer Kit has 36 complete kits; other instruments play one sound chromatically or in scale.
 
-1. [Install](#1-install)
-2. [Learn the controls](#2-learn-the-controls)
-3. [Select a track](#3-select-a-track)
-4. [Load samples into a kit](#4-load-samples-into-a-kit)
-5. [Edit a pad](#5-edit-a-pad)
-6. [Record a beat](#6-record-a-beat)
-7. [Add a plug-in instrument](#7-add-a-plug-in-instrument)
-8. [Save the project](#8-save-the-project)
-9. [Exit Rhythmer](#9-exit-rhythmer)
+Press SEQ for PATTERNS. Hold SHIFT and press B3 GEN. Select GENERATE SONG to assign a kit and three instruments to tracks 1–4, 5–8, 9–12 or 13–16. GEN SETUP changes the target or chooses MIDI-only tracks. GENERATE TRACK keeps the selected instrument. Turn the seed to reproduce a pattern. BACK returns from Acid/Break to GEN, then PATTERNS.
 
-## 1. Install
+Stage B1 shows PRESETS with the engine artwork and its real filter or representative sound controls; B1 again opens EDIT. B2 opens PERFORM (DJ FILTER / ECHO / SPACE), then ARP / CHORD. Rhythmer Kit has its own whole-kit filter, saved with its presets; KIT labels mean all pads and P11 labels mean pad 11. Sample Kit / Break land on SOUND with their existing whole-track filter, followed by TRIM. The encoder or −/+ moves native parameter rows; K1–K3 edit the highlighted controls. In Edit, B3 opens SAVE (Rhythmer Kit cycles SOURCE / SAVE / EDIT). SHIFT+B3 toggles plug-in TRANSPORT. Double-tap STOP cuts all audio.
 
-You need:
+New plug-ins go in Rhythmer/Plugins on the card. Existing top-level Plugins remain readable. Use the device page or Files over USB at http://rhythmer.local. Firmware updates must be signed Rhythmer OS releases.
 
-- An Akai MPC Sample with firmware **1.3.0.12**. On any other firmware
-  Rhythmer does not start and the stock app keeps running.
-- A microSD card.
-- The release zip, `Rhythmer-MPC-Sample-<version>.zip`.
+Based on Melodee by Kerem Kiliç (Ellic Studio). Developed by jazzy rhythmer.
 
-The zip holds one folder, `autorun`. Its `README.txt` and the licences are
-inside it, in `autorun/rhythmer/`.
+## Start from an empty track or pad
 
-To install Rhythmer:
+Press SAMPLE, then use SOUND or TRIM. On a completely empty Sample Kit, Push the encoder to open TRACK TYPE: PLUG-IN opens the instrument browser; SAMPLE KIT opens the first-sample browser. On a selected empty pad with samples elsewhere in the kit, Push opens SAMPLES for that pad. Select a file and Push to load it. Hitting another pad in the browser changes the destination, so check the selected pad before loading. All 128 pads and secondary layers count as existing content.
 
-1. Back up the card. If it has an `autorun` folder at its top level, move
-   that folder somewhere safe. Rhythmer's `autorun` folder replaces it.
-2. Unzip the release and copy the `autorun` folder to the top level of the
-   card. The card now has `autorun/autorun.sh` and `autorun/rhythmer/`. Do
-   not edit or rename anything inside `autorun`: the MPC does not start an
-   autorun whose files have changed.
-3. Optional: to use plug-ins, make a folder named `Plugins` inside the
-   `Rhythmer` folder on the card (`Rhythmer/Plugins`) and copy your plug-ins
-   into it. A plug-in's release zip can go in as it is: Rhythmer unzips it
-   the next time the plug-in picker opens. See
-   [Plug-ins](guide/plug-ins.md) for what runs.
-4. Put the card in the MPC and switch it on. The stock app starts first. A
-   few seconds later Rhythmer starts.
+The face shows PUSH: TRACK TYPE or PUSH: LOAD SAMPLE. SHIFT + Push closes the browser and returns to its caller. B1 goes up a folder, or returns to the caller at the browser root. SHIFT + Minus undoes a sample assignment. A never-assigned or intentional EMPTY track retains the native type carousel. Loaded pads, other edit pages and Break loop loading retain their existing clicks. Use TRACKS → B1 TRACK SETUP for other instrument/type changes and track deletion.
 
-Rhythmer changes nothing on the MPC itself. To stop it from starting, delete
-the `autorun` folder from the card.
+## Preset browsing
 
-While Rhythmer runs, connect the MPC to a computer with USB-C and open
-**http://melodee.local** in a browser. The page installs plug-ins and
-updates, moves files to and from the card, and holds this quickstart and
-the user guide. To update Rhythmer later, see
-[Update Rhythmer](guide/projects-and-files.md#update-rhythmer).
-
-## 2. Learn the controls
-
-The printed buttons keep their MPC meaning. The jobs printed under the pads
-are **SHIFT** + pad, as on the stock app. The map below shows what each
-button does in Rhythmer.
-
-![The MPC Sample's controls in Rhythmer](images/guide/panel.png)
-
-Every page uses the same layout:
-
-![The parts of a Rhythmer page](images/guide/screen.png)
-
-These controls work the same on every page:
-
-| Control | Action |
-| --- | --- |
-| **B1**, **B2**, **B3** | Select the page or action named above each key. |
-| **K1**, **K2**, **K3** | Set the value on the card above each knob. |
-| Encoder (turn) | Move through a list, or fine-tune the outlined card. |
-| Encoder (push) | Open the item under the cursor, or move to the next card. |
-| **SHIFT** + encoder push | Go back one page. |
-| **SHIFT** + **−** / **+** | Undo / redo. |
-
-## 3. Select a track
-
-Rhythmer has 16 tracks, one for each pad. Pad 1 (bottom left) is track 1.
-
-To select a track, hold **PAD BANK** and press a pad. This works on any
-page.
-
-A new project has an empty kit on track 1. The other tracks are empty until
-you choose what they are (see [step 7](#7-add-a-plug-in-instrument)).
-
-To see all tracks as a mixer, press **PAD FX** and **KNOB FX** together to
-open **Tracks**.
-Each cell shows a track's number, its pattern, its type and its level. Use
-**K2** to set the selected track's level and **K3** to set its pan.
-
-![The Tracks page](images/screens/tracks.png)
-
-## 4. Load samples into a kit
-
-Rhythmer reads WAV (16, 24 or 32-bit), MP3, FLAC, Ogg Vorbis and AIFF files (any sample rate,
-up to 60 seconds) from a folder named `Samples` at the top level of the card. It can
-also read the MPC's internal factory samples.
-
-1. Select track 1 (hold **PAD BANK**, press pad 1).
-2. Press **SAMPLE SELECT**. The sample browser opens.
-3. Turn the encoder to move through the list. Push the encoder to open a
-   folder. Press **B1** to go back out of a folder.
-4. Press **B2** to switch between the card (**CARD**) and the MPC's
-   factory samples (**INTERNAL**).
-5. Press **B3** to turn on **PREVIEW**. Each file plays when you move to it.
-6. Hit the pad you want to load onto, then push the encoder on a file. The
-   file loads onto the last pad you hit.
-
-To load a file onto the next empty pad, hold **SHIFT** and press any pad.
-
-![The sample browser](images/screens/samples.png)
-
-The browser also loads SFZ, MPC programs and expansions, EXS24, SoundFont
-and DecentSampler instruments onto a pad. See
-[Sampled instruments](guide/kits-and-sampling.md#sampled-instruments).
-
-## 5. Edit a pad
-
-Press **SAMPLE** to open **Stage**. Stage holds the quick pages of the
-selected track. On a kit, these are the stock Sample mode pages for the last
-pad you hit.
-
-![Stage on a kit: TRIM](images/screens/trim.png)
-
-- **B1** cycles **TRIM**, **LAYERS**, **TUNE** and **AMP ENV** (on a sampled
-  instrument: **ZONES**, **TUNE** and **AMP ENV**).
-- **B2** cycles **PLAY**, **COLOUR**, **FOLLOW** and **CLOUD**.
-- **B3** cycles **MIX**, **SENDS**, **FILTER**, **FILT ENV** and **KIT FILT**.
-
-Press the lit key again to go to its next page. The dots under a key show
-which page of its cycle is open.
-
-On **TRIM**, use **K1** to set the start point, **K2** the end point and
-**K3** the loop point. Hold **SHIFT** and turn a knob to zoom in at that
-point.
-
-To chop a sample into slices, press **CHOP**. See [Chop](guide/kits-and-sampling.md#chop).
-
-## 6. Record a beat
-
-1. Press **SEQ** to open **Patterns**. If Roll or Motion opens instead,
-   press **B1** (**PATTERNS**). The selected track's 16 patterns of the
-   bank in view (**BANK A**) are laid out as the pads: pad 1 bottom left.
-2. Use **K1** to set the pattern length in bars, **K2** the grid (Q) and
-   **K3** the swing.
-3. To choose a pattern, press its pad. Pad 1 is pattern 1. On other pages,
-   hold **SEQ** and press a pad.
-
-   ![Patterns](images/screens/patterns.png)
-
-4. Press **SEQ RECORD**. The button flashes and the screen shows that
-   recording is armed.
-5. Press **PLAY**. Recording starts. Play the pads.
-
-   ![SEQ RECORD armed](images/screens/recarmed.png)
-
-6. Press **SEQ RECORD** again to stop recording. Playback continues.
-7. Press **STOP** to stop.
-
-Each take is one undo step. Press **SHIFT** + **−** to undo it.
-
-Recording options:
-
-- **SHIFT** + **Pad 4**: turn the one-bar count-in on or off.
-- **SHIFT** + **Pad 10**: open **Rec Quantize**. Press **B3** to turn it on
-  or off, and turn the encoder to choose the grid.
-- **SHIFT** + **TAP TEMPO**: set the metronome to Off, On or Rec.
-
-To edit the notes, press **B2** (**ROLL**) for the piano roll, or **SHIFT** +
-**SEQ** for **Step Edit**. In Step Edit, press **SHIFT** + **B1** (**PADS**)
-for **STEPS** mode: each pad sets or clears a step of the bar. On a kit,
-STEPS edits the last pad you hit.
-
-![Step Edit in STEPS mode](images/screens/stepeditsteps.png)
-
-## 7. Add a plug-in instrument
-
-Rhythmer loads VST3, LV2, CLAP and VST2 instruments built for the MPC's ARM processor,
-including the Melodee Poly, Melodee PD and Melodee Chip synths. Put them in
-the `Rhythmer/Plugins` folder on the card first (see [step 1](#1-install)). The
-Rhythmer synths are free downloads; see [Plug-ins](guide/plug-ins.md).
-
-1. Hold **PAD BANK** and press pad 2 to select track 2.
-2. The track is empty, so Stage opens with a row of cards for what it
-   becomes: **SYNTH** (a plug-in instrument), **KIT** (an empty kit,
-   samples from the card, or a recording) and **MIDI** (an external
-   instrument on the MIDI Out jack or USB).
-
-   ![Stage on an empty track](images/screens/stageemptysynth.png)
-
-3. Turn the encoder to **SYNTH** and push it. The plug-in picker opens on
-   the `Rhythmer/Plugins` folder.
-4. Turn the encoder to a plug-in and push the encoder to load it.
-   Plug-ins that cannot run on the MPC are dimmed. Once it loads, Rhythmer
-   goes back to the page you were on.
-
-   ![The plug-in picker](images/screens/plugins.png)
-
-5. Press **SAMPLE** to open Stage, and play the pads. To set the key and
-   scale the pads play in, hold **SAMPLE** to see **Keys** and turn **K1**
-   for the root, **K2** for the scale and **K3** for the pad layout. Press
-   **−** / **+** to change the octave.
-
-   ![Keys](images/screens/keys.png)
-
-6. Press **SAMPLE** again for **PRESETS**, the first page of **B1**. Turn
-   the encoder to step through the plug-in's presets, or push it for the
-   whole list. **K1**–**K3** are **FILTER**, **ECHO** and **SPACE** on
-   every plug-in.
-
-   ![Stage PRESETS on a plug-in track](images/screens/stagepluginpresets.png)
-
-7. Press **B1** for **EDIT**, its next page: the plug-in's own parameters
-   come on **K1**–**K3**. Turn the encoder or press **−** / **+** to move
-   through the rows.
-
-   ![Stage EDIT: a plug-in's parameters](images/screens/stagepluginedit.png)
-
-Record the plug-in track the same way as the kit in
-[step 6](#6-record-a-beat).
-
-## 8. Save the project
-
-1. Press **SHIFT** + **Pad 16** to open **Project**.
-2. Press **B1** (**SAVE**).
-
-![Project: SAVE, OPEN, NEW](images/screens/project.png)
-
-The first time you save, Rhythmer asks for a name. The pads type like phone
-keys: each pad shows the letter it types next. Pad 14 types a space, pad 15
-switches to digits and pad 16 deletes. Turn the encoder to move the cursor.
-Press **B3** (**SAVE**) or push the encoder to save. Press **B1** to cancel.
-
-![Naming a project](images/screens/nameproject.png)
-
-Projects are saved in `Rhythmer/Projects` on the card. To open another
-project, press **B2** (**OPEN**) on the Project page.
-
-## 9. Exit Rhythmer
-
-Press **POWER** briefly. The Exit screen opens:
-
-- **B1** (**STAY**): go back to Rhythmer.
-- **B2** (**POWER OFF**): save the project and switch the MPC off.
-- **B3** (**MPC APP**): save the project and go back to the stock app until
-  the next time the MPC is switched on.
-
-![The Exit screen](images/screens/exitcard.png)
-
-When Rhythmer starts again, it opens the project you had open.
-
